WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.429 --> 00:00:07.410
&gt;&gt;

00:00:07.429 --> 00:00:08.429
[Applause]

00:00:08.429 --> 00:00:10.959
Carlos Ghosn: It's better always to enjoy applause before

00:00:10.979 --> 00:00:12.330
than after.

00:00:12.349 --> 00:00:13.330
&gt;&gt;

00:00:13.349 --> 00:00:14.349
[Laughing]

00:00:14.349 --> 00:00:16.600
SPEAKER02: Mr. Ghosn, thank you for joining us today.

00:00:16.539 --> 00:00:19.289
I would like to open by asking you how you approach

00:00:18.939 --> 00:00:19.939
leadership,

00:00:19.939 --> 00:00:23.289
strategy, and execution differently at Nissan versus at

00:00:23.309 --> 00:00:24.309
Renault, given

00:00:24.309 --> 00:00:27.009
that each company has very different cultural contexts.

00:00:27.029 --> 00:00:33.059
Carlos Ghosn: Well, you know, the French -- the French way

00:00:33.079 --> 00:00:35.219
of

00:00:35.239 --> 00:00:38.749
managing and the leadership in French expresses itself in a

00:00:38.769 --> 00:00:39.769
completely

00:00:39.769 --> 00:00:42.669
different terms than Japan.

00:00:42.689 --> 00:00:45.289
I knew it from the beginning.

00:00:45.309 --> 00:00:48.489
So in a certain way you have some fundamentals which are the

00:00:48.509 --> 00:00:49.509
same,

00:00:49.509 --> 00:00:54.959
umm, and we're gonna probably talk about what are these

00:00:54.979 --> 00:00:55.979
fundamentals

00:00:55.979 --> 00:01:01.539
but the way you exercise these fundamentals are completely -

00:01:01.559 --> 00:01:01.759
-

00:01:01.759 --> 00:01:04.150
completely different.

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:07.670
In Japan, I don't run meetings the same way I run them in

00:01:07.569 --> 00:01:09.329
France.

00:01:09.349 --> 00:01:13.239
I don't reward people the same way than I do within France

00:01:13.259 --> 00:01:14.259
and what is

00:01:14.259 --> 00:01:17.259
expected with me in term of communication we don't do the

00:01:16.459 --> 00:01:17.459
same things

00:01:17.459 --> 00:01:18.459
in Japan.

00:01:17.959 --> 00:01:21.250
They are not -- the tools are not the same, the words are

00:01:21.269 --> 00:01:22.269
not the

00:01:22.269 --> 00:01:25.269
same, the way even you shape your strategy's not the same.

00:01:25.039 --> 00:01:28.539
So what we have to do when you are in a situation where you'

00:01:28.369 --> 00:01:29.369
re

00:01:29.369 --> 00:01:32.019
managing two different culture is you want to make sure

00:01:32.039 --> 00:01:33.500
about what is

00:01:33.519 --> 00:01:36.909
the content, which usually is very common, and then, what is

00:01:36.929 --> 00:01:37.929
the

00:01:37.929 --> 00:01:40.909
packaging of the content which has to take into

00:01:40.929 --> 00:01:42.060
consideration with how

00:01:42.079 --> 00:01:43.079
they consideration the culture.

00:01:43.079 --> 00:01:46.859
And I can tell you that when we're talking about France and

00:01:46.879 --> 00:01:48.299
Japan but

00:01:48.319 --> 00:01:52.939
it's varied between the United States, or China, or India.

00:01:52.959 --> 00:01:55.709
Every time you have to make sure about many difference about

00:01:55.479 --> 00:01:56.479
what's

00:01:56.479 --> 00:01:59.239
the content in what do I need to do?

00:01:59.259 --> 00:02:01.009
What is the essence of my message?

00:02:01.009 --> 00:02:03.759
And, second, what is the best way, what is the most

00:02:03.419 --> 00:02:04.419
efficient way to

00:02:04.419 --> 00:02:06.799
make this message go through?

00:02:06.819 --> 00:02:10.659
SPEAKER02: When you joined Nissan in 1999, the company had

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:11.680
been

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:14.829
suffering from major losses since 1973 and only three of its

00:02:14.849 --> 00:02:15.849
48 models

00:02:15.849 --> 00:02:16.969
were profitable.

00:02:16.989 --> 00:02:19.239
You turned the company around and restored it to

00:02:18.699 --> 00:02:19.699
profitability within

00:02:19.699 --> 00:02:20.779
two years.

00:02:20.799 --> 00:02:23.549
As both the company outsider and the first foreign CEO of

00:02:23.549 --> 00:02:24.549
the company,

00:02:24.549 --> 00:02:27.549
how did you earn the support of your team and motivate them

00:02:27.079 --> 00:02:28.079
to execute

00:02:28.079 --> 00:02:29.079
on your plan?

00:02:28.639 --> 00:02:32.169
Carlos Ghosn: Well, you know, 1999 the situation was really

00:02:32.189 --> 00:02:33.189
bad in

00:02:33.189 --> 00:02:37.439
Nissan and when you are, you know, taking responsibility for

00:02:37.459 --> 00:02:38.459
a

00:02:38.459 --> 00:02:41.689
situation which is bad it's -- it also is France because we

00:02:41.709 --> 00:02:42.709
don't know

00:02:42.709 --> 00:02:45.209
to explain the situation to people that they know already.

00:02:44.959 --> 00:02:45.959
They know that.

00:02:45.959 --> 00:02:46.159
&gt;&gt;

00:02:45.959 --> 00:02:46.959
[Laughing]

00:02:45.959 --> 00:02:51.109
Carlos Ghosn: And you need to know also that the solution is

00:02:51.129 --> 00:02:52.129
always

00:02:52.129 --> 00:02:53.129
here.

00:02:52.379 --> 00:02:55.879
We don't is to look -- we don't need to invent a solution.

00:02:55.379 --> 00:02:57.879
We know that people know already that it's bad.

00:02:57.629 --> 00:03:00.429
And second, that the solution exists but it's buried inside

00:03:00.449 --> 00:03:01.449
the

00:03:01.449 --> 00:03:02.449
company.

00:03:02.359 --> 00:03:07.099
So your job is very simple in a certain way, is just make

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:08.120
sure that

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:11.369
you make the very lucid diagnosis of the situation.

00:03:11.389 --> 00:03:12.389
Very lucid.

00:03:12.389 --> 00:03:16.099
No emotion, no, you know, sugar coating, no politics, no

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:17.120
complacency.

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:24.029
Extremely lucid assessment of the situation and listen to

00:03:24.049 --> 00:03:25.049
what people

00:03:25.049 --> 00:03:27.399
have to say to a very simple question.

00:03:27.419 --> 00:03:29.559
Why are we in this situation?

00:03:29.579 --> 00:03:31.299
What you think can we improve?

00:03:31.319 --> 00:03:33.319
What are the things that should be done?

00:03:32.569 --> 00:03:36.569
Then you have your own personal doing but with other

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:37.590
priorities

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:40.839
because you end up with a laundry list of measures that

00:03:40.859 --> 00:03:41.859
needs to be

00:03:41.859 --> 00:03:45.309
done and obviously you cannot work on 120 objective or on

00:03:45.329 --> 00:03:46.329
200

00:03:46.329 --> 00:03:47.329
objective.

00:03:47.049 --> 00:03:49.549
You need really to concentrate them into two or three

00:03:48.979 --> 00:03:49.979
because that's

00:03:49.979 --> 00:03:52.729
the only thing you can absorb at the level of big

00:03:52.399 --> 00:03:53.399
organization.

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:56.649
Make sure they are the right one and start to work on them.

00:03:56.519 --> 00:04:00.199
So, you know, in Nissan, in 1999, everybody knew that Nissan

00:04:00.219 --> 00:04:01.219
had the

00:04:01.219 --> 00:04:02.219
problem.

00:04:01.609 --> 00:04:06.159
The only thing that nobody recognize that the problem was in

00:04:06.179 --> 00:04:07.179
his own

00:04:07.179 --> 00:04:08.179
area.

00:04:08.069 --> 00:04:09.069
You know?

00:04:08.419 --> 00:04:11.419
If I was in sales, I was blaming the product planner that

00:04:11.189 --> 00:04:12.189
they were

00:04:12.189 --> 00:04:14.749
not able to come with a car competitive with Toyota.

00:04:14.769 --> 00:04:18.019
If I was a product planner, I said I have a great product

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:17.920
but the

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:18.920
design is not good.

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:21.670
The designer said what the engineers are messing up with me.

00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:24.750
So everybody in a certain way felt good about what they were

00:04:24.769 --> 00:04:25.769
doing but

00:04:25.769 --> 00:04:27.180
the company had the problem.

00:04:27.199 --> 00:04:29.949
So you need to change this by saying, okay, we understand

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:30.920
that all the

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:34.170
guys are not doing their job but what we want for you is

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:34.920
what you can

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:38.420
do, you know, in your own area, even if you think it's not

00:04:37.419 --> 00:04:38.419
very

00:04:38.419 --> 00:04:41.419
important, what you can do in your own area in order to

00:04:40.919 --> 00:04:41.919
solve -- to

00:04:41.919 --> 00:04:42.919
solve the problem.

00:04:42.669 --> 00:04:49.230
So lucid diagnosis, no complacency, finding the bits of

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:50.250
solution

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:53.740
inside the company, put them in perspective, put them into

00:04:53.759 --> 00:04:55.100
priorities,

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:57.120
put it in a way which is attractive.

00:04:56.419 --> 00:04:57.419
You know?

00:04:57.419 --> 00:04:59.709
Because what is management about?

00:04:59.729 --> 00:05:02.540
Management and particularly leadership is about asking

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:03.560
people to do

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:05.560
things that they do not want to do.

00:05:05.399 --> 00:05:06.399
That's it.

00:05:06.399 --> 00:05:07.399
That's management.

00:05:06.899 --> 00:05:07.099
&gt;&gt;

00:05:06.899 --> 00:05:07.899
[Laughing]

00:05:06.899 --> 00:05:08.899
Carlos Ghosn: That's what it's about.

00:05:08.399 --> 00:05:11.149
I mean, you don't manage a situation where everything is

00:05:10.149 --> 00:05:11.149
okay.

00:05:11.149 --> 00:05:12.149
You know?

00:05:11.649 --> 00:05:12.649
That's not management.

00:05:12.399 --> 00:05:14.540
That's supervision, that's administration.

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:16.639
What's really management and leadership?

00:05:16.659 --> 00:05:18.909
You're gonna ask -- you're gonna have -- okay.

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:21.259
Say people don't want to cut head count.

00:05:21.279 --> 00:05:24.819
They don't want to restructure, they want to, uh, you know,

00:05:24.839 --> 00:05:25.839
close down

00:05:25.839 --> 00:05:29.839
plants, they don't want to retreat from market where they

00:05:29.859 --> 00:05:30.859
have been

00:05:30.859 --> 00:05:33.609
for many years, they don't want to stop some activities,

00:05:32.859 --> 00:05:33.859
they don't

00:05:33.859 --> 00:05:34.859
want to sell assets.

00:05:34.859 --> 00:05:36.359
They don't wanna do that.

00:05:35.359 --> 00:05:36.359
Okay?

00:05:36.359 --> 00:05:39.109
So the very simple question of management is, how do you

00:05:38.859 --> 00:05:39.859
bring them to

00:05:39.859 --> 00:05:44.949
do this, and keep their motivation, and be convinced of

00:05:44.969 --> 00:05:45.970
doing the

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:46.990
right thing?

00:05:46.519 --> 00:05:48.490
That's management and that's leadership.

00:05:48.509 --> 00:05:52.310
And for this, the basic element is, put it in perspective,

00:05:52.329 --> 00:05:53.519
give

00:05:53.539 --> 00:05:56.509
yourself an objective that everybody say, oh, that's what we

00:05:56.529 --> 00:05:57.529
want to

00:05:57.529 --> 00:06:00.980
achieve so it helps them go through a tough situation where

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:02.000
they will

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:05.750
do things that they don't want to do but they know it's for

00:06:04.539 --> 00:06:05.539
the -- for

00:06:05.539 --> 00:06:06.539
the right thing.

00:06:06.289 --> 00:06:07.539
And this is Nissan story.

00:06:07.539 --> 00:06:09.039
That's exactly the Nissan story.

00:06:08.789 --> 00:06:11.980
You know, when I arrive in Japan, 1999, one of the reason

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:13.000
for which

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:16.000
Nissan was in trouble was there was a lot of decision which

00:06:15.289 --> 00:06:16.289
needed to

00:06:16.289 --> 00:06:19.220
be taken five years ago were not taken.

00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:22.740
But a lot of people used to tell you, you know, you are in

00:06:22.199 --> 00:06:23.199
Japan, you

00:06:23.199 --> 00:06:25.699
cannot close a plant, you cannot reduce head count, you

00:06:25.199 --> 00:06:26.199
cannot undo

00:06:26.199 --> 00:06:28.439
cross share holding, you cannot touch the

00:06:28.459 --> 00:06:29.459
[inaudible], you cannot

00:06:29.459 --> 00:06:31.709
touch the seniority system, you cannot, you cannot, you

00:06:31.399 --> 00:06:32.399
cannot do.

00:06:32.399 --> 00:06:35.399
You had a lot of thing that is nobody wanted to touch.

00:06:35.399 --> 00:06:38.329
So there was absolutely no way you gonna fix the company

00:06:38.349 --> 00:06:39.349
without

00:06:39.349 --> 00:06:41.269
touching all these taboos.

00:06:41.289 --> 00:06:43.360
So we start to say, okay, look.

00:06:43.379 --> 00:06:46.629
Are we all committed to say we're gonna come back to profit

00:06:45.810 --> 00:06:46.810
and we're

00:06:46.810 --> 00:06:48.060
gonna grow this company again?

00:06:47.310 --> 00:06:48.310
Yes.

00:06:48.310 --> 00:06:49.310
No doubt.

00:06:48.810 --> 00:06:49.810
Unanimity.

00:06:49.509 --> 00:06:50.509
Okay?

00:06:49.839 --> 00:06:53.089
Let's commit to this, we all commit to this and say, okay,

00:06:52.879 --> 00:06:53.879
now we're

00:06:53.879 --> 00:06:57.129
gonna start to explain what is the role and as you know the

00:06:56.379 --> 00:06:57.379
Nissan

00:06:57.379 --> 00:06:59.629
revival plan challenge every single taboo because you done

00:06:58.879 --> 00:06:59.879
everything

00:06:59.879 --> 00:07:02.879
which was forbidden and people say you would not be able to

00:07:02.229 --> 00:07:03.229
do but

00:07:03.229 --> 00:07:05.910
with clear commitment to return to profitability in the

00:07:05.930 --> 00:07:07.019
first year --

00:07:07.039 --> 00:07:08.789
within the first year of the plant.

00:07:08.649 --> 00:07:11.149
So that's the way you drive people, you know?

00:07:10.899 --> 00:07:12.399
That's what management is about.

00:07:12.149 --> 00:07:15.149
Put in front of them something that they want really to do,

00:07:14.729 --> 00:07:15.729
to

00:07:15.729 --> 00:07:18.759
achieve, that is really significant for them.

00:07:18.779 --> 00:07:20.610
Significant for them not only theoretically but

00:07:20.629 --> 00:07:22.069
pragmatically they are

00:07:22.089 --> 00:07:25.120
all connected with this victory that they are proud of

00:07:25.139 --> 00:07:26.139
having revived

00:07:26.139 --> 00:07:29.139
the company but it was good for them for their salary, for

00:07:27.579 --> 00:07:28.579
their

00:07:28.579 --> 00:07:31.160
career, for their compensation, for their stock options, for

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:32.180
their

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:33.920
benefits, for their retirement, for everything.

00:07:33.939 --> 00:07:37.279
Then after you align this now you say, now we have to lose

00:07:37.299 --> 00:07:38.299
jobs.

00:07:38.299 --> 00:07:41.360
SPEAKER02: At the end of this year, you are planning to

00:07:41.379 --> 00:07:42.379
launch the

00:07:42.379 --> 00:07:45.279
Nissan Leaf, an electric vehicle that uses lithium ion

00:07:45.299 --> 00:07:46.299
battery

00:07:46.299 --> 00:07:49.049
technology and will be one of the early zero emission cars

00:07:48.879 --> 00:07:49.879
on the

00:07:49.879 --> 00:07:50.879
market.

00:07:50.389 --> 00:07:51.389
Carlos Ghosn: Mm.

00:07:51.139 --> 00:07:53.139
SPEAKER02: Incidentally, as part of our first-year

00:07:52.519 --> 00:07:53.519
curriculum, we

00:07:53.519 --> 00:07:56.019
watched the movie "Who Killed the Electric Car" and I

00:07:55.739 --> 00:07:56.739
understand that

00:07:56.739 --> 00:07:59.489
you're collaborating with that movie's producers to create a

00:07:58.759 --> 00:07:59.759
sequel

00:07:59.759 --> 00:08:01.500
called "Revenge of the Electric Car".

00:08:01.519 --> 00:08:01.719
&gt;&gt;

00:08:01.719 --> 00:08:02.719
[Laughing]

00:08:01.719 --> 00:08:02.969
Carlos Ghosn: It's true.

00:08:02.519 --> 00:08:02.719
&gt;&gt;

00:08:02.719 --> 00:08:03.719
[Laughing]

00:08:02.719 --> 00:08:04.219
Carlos Ghosn: No, it is true.

00:08:04.189 --> 00:08:05.189
It is true.

00:08:05.189 --> 00:08:06.689
There are a film like that.

00:08:06.689 --> 00:08:09.689
We spend many hours with them and they came to Tokyo, and

00:08:09.189 --> 00:08:10.189
they filmed

00:08:10.189 --> 00:08:13.189
the car, and hopefully it's going to be an interesting one.

00:08:12.939 --> 00:08:15.189
SPEAKER02: What is your strategy for driving adoption and

00:08:14.689 --> 00:08:15.689
becoming a

00:08:15.689 --> 00:08:18.439
leader in the electric vehicle market in the U.S. and

00:08:17.689 --> 00:08:18.689
globally?

00:08:18.689 --> 00:08:21.189
Carlos Ghosn: Well, you know, first, if you want to

00:08:21.039 --> 00:08:22.089
innovate, if you

00:08:22.109 --> 00:08:24.859
want to innovate, you have to accept from the beginning that

00:08:24.589 --> 00:08:25.589
a lot of

00:08:25.589 --> 00:08:28.589
people are gonna think that you're a fool, you're playing

00:08:27.429 --> 00:08:28.429
with

00:08:28.429 --> 00:08:31.679
shareholders' money, you're taking bets that should not be

00:08:31.699 --> 00:08:32.699
taken, that

00:08:32.699 --> 00:08:35.449
there would never work, etc. etc. and that's exactly what

00:08:35.149 --> 00:08:36.149
we're

00:08:36.149 --> 00:08:37.149
hearing today.

00:08:36.730 --> 00:08:39.220
That's exactly what I'm reading today.

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:42.850
And it's absolutely unbelievable, unbelievable to see how

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:43.870
much

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:47.529
short-sighted, how much short-sighted -- probably the media

00:08:47.549 --> 00:08:48.549
and a lot

00:08:48.549 --> 00:08:52.009
of analysts are about what we are -- how we understand the

00:08:52.029 --> 00:08:53.029
situation

00:08:53.029 --> 00:08:55.370
in which the car industry is.

00:08:55.389 --> 00:08:57.970
So we decided, after analyzing everything to say, okay, zero

00:08:57.990 --> 00:08:58.990
emission

00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:00.240
is the way to go.

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:03.490
Doesn't mean that all the cars are going to be zero emission

00:09:02.740 --> 00:09:03.740
but there

00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:06.240
is a huge and tremendous boulevard for the development of

00:09:05.740 --> 00:09:06.740
the zero

00:09:06.740 --> 00:09:09.740
emission cars and we can spend a lot of time explain that

00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:10.240
but anyway

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:12.490
obviously today people -- we've invested already $6 billion

00:09:12.159 --> 00:09:13.159
on this

00:09:13.159 --> 00:09:16.360
project and people say, well, you know what?

00:09:16.379 --> 00:09:21.830
If this is not gonna be a big success it's gonna be a

00:09:21.850 --> 00:09:22.850
tremendous -- a

00:09:22.850 --> 00:09:24.850
tremendous way on the performance, the financial performance

00:09:24.329 --> 00:09:25.329
of the

00:09:25.329 --> 00:09:26.649
company.

00:09:26.669 --> 00:09:29.919
First, I think it's going to be a tremendous success and I

00:09:28.389 --> 00:09:29.389
think this

00:09:29.389 --> 00:09:33.139
is going to be the way of the future and we can spend a lot

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:33.500
of time

00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:36.750
explaining it but what I'm gonna tell you is that, umm, we

00:09:36.250 --> 00:09:37.250
are in the

00:09:37.250 --> 00:09:38.500
final phase before the launch.

00:09:38.509 --> 00:09:40.759
The launch will come by the end of 2010.

00:09:40.679 --> 00:09:43.679
In fact, it's gonna be mass marketed in the United States

00:09:43.370 --> 00:09:44.370
starting

00:09:44.370 --> 00:09:49.909
November or December 2010, the same time in -- in Japan.

00:09:49.929 --> 00:09:52.809
I understand that even we showed the Leaf in Stanford

00:09:52.829 --> 00:09:53.860
campus.

00:09:53.879 --> 00:09:55.629
Professor, I think you've driven it.

00:09:55.089 --> 00:09:59.509
I mean, the only -- you have to go into this car, drive it

00:09:59.529 --> 00:10:00.529
to

00:10:00.529 --> 00:10:02.259
understand that's who we are.

00:10:02.279 --> 00:10:06.429
That's not the kind of enhanced golf cart, you know, where

00:10:06.449 --> 00:10:07.449
you have to

00:10:07.449 --> 00:10:07.649
--

00:10:07.449 --> 00:10:07.649
&gt;&gt;

00:10:07.449 --> 00:10:08.449
[Laughing]

00:10:07.449 --> 00:10:10.699
Carlos Ghosn: -- this is a real car and on top of this, the

00:10:10.379 --> 00:10:11.379
basic

00:10:11.379 --> 00:10:14.879
assumption is, it's affordable, makes a lot of sense, and

00:10:14.899 --> 00:10:15.899
we're

00:10:15.899 --> 00:10:17.649
offering the zero emission as a premium.

00:10:17.649 --> 00:10:20.399
We're not asking consumer to pay for the zero emission.

00:10:19.899 --> 00:10:20.899
That doesn't work.

00:10:20.899 --> 00:10:23.649
Is you gonna get the zero emission as -- as a premium.

00:10:23.649 --> 00:10:26.899
So, again, you have to have a vision, this vision has to be

00:10:26.689 --> 00:10:27.689
based on

00:10:27.689 --> 00:10:31.029
understanding about the dynamics of the market, globally,

00:10:31.049 --> 00:10:32.049
and then you

00:10:32.049 --> 00:10:33.299
have to pursue this vision.

00:10:33.299 --> 00:10:35.799
No matter what you have to build motivation inside your

00:10:35.529 --> 00:10:36.529
company.

00:10:36.529 --> 00:10:39.529
This is easy because you're saying, okay, we wanna be bigger

00:10:38.789 --> 00:10:39.789
and a

00:10:39.789 --> 00:10:42.289
technology that is meaningful to the consumer and all the

00:10:41.529 --> 00:10:42.529
Nissan

00:10:42.529 --> 00:10:44.779
people, all the Renault people are buying into it.

00:10:44.779 --> 00:10:48.029
Then we need to come to the consumer and tell him, you know,

00:10:47.669 --> 00:10:48.669
tell the

00:10:48.669 --> 00:10:51.419
consumer, that's a great product which is affordable and on

00:10:51.110 --> 00:10:52.110
top of

00:10:52.110 --> 00:10:56.230
this is gonna allow you to drive without the guilt of the

00:10:56.250 --> 00:10:57.250
melting of

00:10:57.250 --> 00:10:59.819
the icebergs, and the change of the seasons, and the

00:10:59.839 --> 00:11:00.839
temperature, etc.

00:11:00.839 --> 00:11:04.370
Umm, I think it's gonna be very powerful.

00:11:04.389 --> 00:11:07.750
But again, before it starts, there's always a doubt.

00:11:07.769 --> 00:11:11.269
And now we are at the period of time where a lot of people

00:11:10.519 --> 00:11:11.519
are

00:11:11.519 --> 00:11:14.769
throwing at you a lot of stones by saying, that's not gonna

00:11:14.329 --> 00:11:15.329
work, and

00:11:15.329 --> 00:11:18.079
then you have a lot of comments from competitors saying, you

00:11:16.689 --> 00:11:17.689
know,

00:11:17.689 --> 00:11:18.939
you're too much rubbish.

00:11:18.689 --> 00:11:19.689
Is not gonna work.

00:11:19.689 --> 00:11:21.939
But honestly, what do you want competitors to say?

00:11:21.939 --> 00:11:23.939
Is this -- he's in the right direction?

00:11:23.439 --> 00:11:24.439
I say, okay.

00:11:24.439 --> 00:11:24.639
&gt;&gt;

00:11:24.439 --> 00:11:25.439
[Laughing]

00:11:24.439 --> 00:11:26.189
Carlos Ghosn: He is the right direction.

00:11:26.189 --> 00:11:27.439
And where is your car?

00:11:27.439 --> 00:11:29.439
I have no idea where is your car.

00:11:29.189 --> 00:11:30.189
What's your situation?

00:11:30.189 --> 00:11:30.389
&gt;&gt;

00:11:30.189 --> 00:11:31.189
[Laughing]

00:11:30.189 --> 00:11:30.389
&gt;&gt;

00:11:30.189 --> 00:11:31.189
[Clapping]

00:11:30.189 --> 00:11:38.549
Carlos Ghosn: I'm absolutely -- I mean, we open -- we open -

00:11:38.569 --> 00:11:39.569
- already

00:11:39.569 --> 00:11:43.569
in the United States we open the possibility for people

00:11:43.589 --> 00:11:44.659
already to

00:11:44.679 --> 00:11:48.009
be -- we want to be on the list for the -- for the electric

00:11:48.029 --> 00:11:50.110
car.

00:11:50.129 --> 00:11:54.340
We had more than 35,000 people already -- I'm not talking

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:55.360
about the

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:56.360
Fiats.

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:59.649
Obviously Fred Smith from Federal Express, and the postal

00:11:59.669 --> 00:12:00.669
services,

00:12:00.669 --> 00:12:03.419
and the electric company all of them want -- want to order

00:12:03.149 --> 00:12:04.149
the car by

00:12:04.149 --> 00:12:05.149
the 10,000s.

00:12:04.899 --> 00:12:06.399
We're not talking about that.

00:12:06.149 --> 00:12:08.899
We're talking about, you know, the people that say, okay,

00:12:08.319 --> 00:12:09.319
this is a

00:12:09.319 --> 00:12:12.069
good thing, and we want it to happen and particularly if

00:12:11.319 --> 00:12:12.319
you're

00:12:12.319 --> 00:12:15.569
telling me it's going to be at the same price than the

00:12:14.819 --> 00:12:15.819
regular car.

00:12:15.819 --> 00:12:17.069
I wanna go for it.

00:12:17.069 --> 00:12:19.319
So I think it's gonna be very powerful.

00:12:19.069 --> 00:12:21.569
Carlos Ghosn: Nissan and Renault have a unique alliance in

00:12:20.819 --> 00:12:21.819
which

00:12:21.819 --> 00:12:24.319
Renault has a 44 percent ownership stake in Nissan, Nissan

00:12:23.819 --> 00:12:24.819
has a

00:12:24.819 --> 00:12:27.819
15 percent ownership stake as Renault, and you act as CEO of

00:12:26.809 --> 00:12:27.809
both

00:12:27.809 --> 00:12:28.809
companies.

00:12:28.679 --> 00:12:31.419
What are the unique opportunities and challenges of this

00:12:31.439 --> 00:12:32.439
relationship

00:12:32.439 --> 00:12:34.689
and how do you handle conflicting interests between Nissan

00:12:33.929 --> 00:12:34.929
and

00:12:34.929 --> 00:12:35.929
Renault?

00:12:35.179 --> 00:12:38.009
Carlos Ghosn: Well, that's a -- that's an interesting --

00:12:38.029 --> 00:12:39.029
that's an

00:12:39.029 --> 00:12:40.509
interesting point.

00:12:40.529 --> 00:12:43.529
You know, we have been -- we have been in this alliance for

00:12:42.269 --> 00:12:43.269
the last

00:12:43.269 --> 00:12:44.269
ten years.

00:12:44.059 --> 00:12:48.860
We are probably the two companies with the most sustainable

00:12:48.879 --> 00:12:49.879
track

00:12:49.879 --> 00:12:52.129
record in term of alliances because practically every single

00:12:52.129 --> 00:12:53.129
other

00:12:53.129 --> 00:12:56.549
alliance that happened in our industry was blown away.

00:12:56.569 --> 00:12:58.870
Everything.

00:12:58.889 --> 00:13:02.120
I remember in 1999 we made the Renault-Nissan alliance

00:13:02.139 --> 00:13:03.139
immediately

00:13:03.139 --> 00:13:04.139
after the DaimlerChrysler alliance.

00:13:04.129 --> 00:13:08.840
Daimler and Chrysler came together and then Renault-Nissan

00:13:08.860 --> 00:13:09.860
came

00:13:09.860 --> 00:13:13.039
together, and then DaimlerChrysler -- of Mitsubishi -- and

00:13:13.059 --> 00:13:14.059
when the

00:13:14.059 --> 00:13:17.759
DaimlerChrysler alliance came together and we came together,

00:13:17.779 --> 00:13:18.779
there was

00:13:18.779 --> 00:13:19.779
a lot of commands.

00:13:19.779 --> 00:13:22.740
DaimlerChrysler was this is an alliance made in heaven.

00:13:22.759 --> 00:13:25.639
Two very rich and powerful company and attractive brands

00:13:25.659 --> 00:13:26.659
coming

00:13:26.659 --> 00:13:29.909
together they're going to do a lot of things and change the

00:13:29.169 --> 00:13:30.169
world.

00:13:30.169 --> 00:13:32.669
And when Renault-Nissan came together to say two mules

00:13:32.449 --> 00:13:33.449
doesn't make

00:13:33.449 --> 00:13:34.449
a -- a horse.

00:13:34.399 --> 00:13:34.600
&gt;&gt;

00:13:34.399 --> 00:13:35.399
[Laughing]

00:13:34.399 --> 00:13:42.939
Carlos Ghosn: Wall Street Journal 1999, I have all the track

00:13:42.959 --> 00:13:43.959
records,

00:13:43.959 --> 00:13:44.959
all the media.

00:13:44.599 --> 00:13:45.629
Everything.

00:13:45.649 --> 00:13:46.649
Okay?

00:13:46.419 --> 00:13:46.620
&gt;&gt;

00:13:46.419 --> 00:13:47.419
[Laughing]

00:13:46.419 --> 00:13:49.169
Carlos Ghosn: Nobody talk about this but we have -- we have

00:13:48.669 --> 00:13:49.669
everything there.

00:13:49.669 --> 00:13:51.009
Okay.

00:13:51.029 --> 00:13:53.779
The two mules started to work and then the two beautiful

00:13:52.909 --> 00:13:53.909
people

00:13:53.909 --> 00:13:57.159
started to work and at the end of the day, after ten years,

00:13:56.419 --> 00:13:59.649
DaimlerChrysler, Mitsubishi, you know the story, and we're

00:13:59.669 --> 00:14:00.669
still

00:14:00.669 --> 00:14:02.809
there.

00:14:02.829 --> 00:14:06.329
Which means that it's better to be a mule than a horse in

00:14:04.730 --> 00:14:05.730
the car

00:14:05.730 --> 00:14:06.730
industry.

00:14:05.980 --> 00:14:06.180
&gt;&gt;

00:14:05.980 --> 00:14:06.980
[Laughing]

00:14:05.980 --> 00:14:08.350
Carlos Ghosn: More resistant.

00:14:08.370 --> 00:14:11.460
More resistant to the shocks and to the problem.

00:14:11.480 --> 00:14:14.980
This is due to the fact -- to the fact that we had a very

00:14:13.750 --> 00:14:14.750
pragmatic

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:15.750
approach.

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:18.480
No grandeur scheme of, you know, we're too different and we'

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:19.500
re gonna

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:22.750
be one, and all the machine are gonna be taken to one place,

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:23.000
and we're

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:24.500
gonna have a superior holding company.

00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:25.250
It doesn't work.

00:14:25.250 --> 00:14:28.250
It doesn't work. We took the alliance as a marriage between

00:14:27.709 --> 00:14:28.709
two

00:14:28.709 --> 00:14:29.709
people.

00:14:29.079 --> 00:14:30.079
Okay?

00:14:29.329 --> 00:14:34.569
When two people marry -- I know that probably some of you

00:14:34.589 --> 00:14:35.649
are not but

00:14:35.669 --> 00:14:40.720
those who have some experience in marriage, uh, nobody want

00:14:40.740 --> 00:14:41.740
become the

00:14:41.740 --> 00:14:43.809
other.

00:14:43.829 --> 00:14:44.829
You know?

00:14:44.349 --> 00:14:47.599
If my wife was saying me we're gonna become one but how

00:14:46.439 --> 00:14:47.439
about you

00:14:47.439 --> 00:14:48.439
become like me?

00:14:48.189 --> 00:14:48.389
&gt;&gt;

00:14:48.189 --> 00:14:49.189
[Laughing]

00:14:48.189 --> 00:14:52.110
Carlos Ghosn: I'm not sure.

00:14:52.129 --> 00:14:55.629
I'm not sure I'm gonna be very happy and exactly the reverse

00:14:54.379 --> 00:14:55.379
same

00:14:55.379 --> 00:14:56.379
thing.

00:14:55.629 --> 00:14:57.379
I'm not gonna ask her that.

00:14:57.129 --> 00:15:00.049
So being different is very important.

00:15:00.069 --> 00:15:01.909
Remaining different is very important.

00:15:01.929 --> 00:15:04.429
Having common goals, having common strategy, but at the same

00:15:04.069 --> 00:15:05.069
time have

00:15:05.069 --> 00:15:07.439
your own autonomy, cultivating things together but even --

00:15:07.459 --> 00:15:08.459
let me --

00:15:08.459 --> 00:15:09.459
this is very important.

00:15:09.459 --> 00:15:13.949
Diversity within uniformity, you know in commonality with

00:15:13.969 --> 00:15:14.969
autonomy.

00:15:14.969 --> 00:15:18.079
That's the way the world works.

00:15:18.099 --> 00:15:21.289
That's the way it works.

00:15:21.309 --> 00:15:24.309
So in a certain way, we try to inspire ourself from the

00:15:23.629 --> 00:15:24.629
basic

00:15:24.629 --> 00:15:28.579
institution of human being -- of human kind by saying, we

00:15:28.599 --> 00:15:29.599
need to make

00:15:29.599 --> 00:15:32.599
sure that, you know, even for the sake of business sense, we

00:15:32.509 --> 00:15:33.509
do not

00:15:33.509 --> 00:15:37.549
violate common sense or human common sense.

00:15:37.569 --> 00:15:39.879
We need to always to maintain, look out.

00:15:39.899 --> 00:15:42.649
And frankly the result has been that even there they have

00:15:42.610 --> 00:15:43.610
been a lot

00:15:43.610 --> 00:15:47.110
of pressure on me to try ask say, why don't you make a

00:15:46.360 --> 00:15:47.360
merger between

00:15:47.360 --> 00:15:50.179
the two company and you don't get one team, etc.?

00:15:50.199 --> 00:15:51.659
It doesn't work.

00:15:51.679 --> 00:15:56.509
I cannot make one team of Japanese and French managing a

00:15:56.529 --> 00:15:57.529
company which

00:15:57.529 --> 00:15:59.029
would be neither Japanese nor French.

00:15:58.990 --> 00:15:59.990
I can't.

00:15:59.990 --> 00:16:02.490
It doesn't work.

00:16:02.509 --> 00:16:04.289
Identity is the basis of motivation.

00:16:04.309 --> 00:16:06.009
Identity is the basis of success.

00:16:06.029 --> 00:16:07.490
It's basis of performance.

00:16:07.509 --> 00:16:09.009
You need to connect to something.

00:16:08.769 --> 00:16:11.769
You need to make sure that you working for your own team,

00:16:10.419 --> 00:16:11.419
for your own

00:16:11.419 --> 00:16:13.129
country, for your own etc.

00:16:13.149 --> 00:16:15.899
You need to belong to something in order to concur the

00:16:15.839 --> 00:16:16.839
world.

00:16:16.839 --> 00:16:20.339
If you don't know why you're doing this, you gonna lose your

00:16:18.719 --> 00:16:19.719
motivation.

00:16:19.719 --> 00:16:23.429
So we have been following this very pragmatic approach.

00:16:23.449 --> 00:16:26.720
Obviously there have a lot of conflicts, there have been a

00:16:26.740 --> 00:16:27.740
lot of

00:16:27.740 --> 00:16:30.240
difference, but every time came back to this common sense

00:16:30.059 --> 00:16:31.059
about, you

00:16:31.059 --> 00:16:34.059
know, if there is no win/win, we don't do it.

00:16:33.559 --> 00:16:36.559
We're not gonna force one decision from one company to the

00:16:35.870 --> 00:16:36.870
other.

00:16:36.870 --> 00:16:39.509
Decisions for Japan -- for Nissan are being taken in Tokyo

00:16:39.529 --> 00:16:40.529
always;

00:16:40.529 --> 00:16:42.899
decision for Renault always taken in Paris.

00:16:42.919 --> 00:16:46.309
Don't confuse the -- the two company but at the same time

00:16:46.329 --> 00:16:47.329
always push

00:16:47.329 --> 00:16:48.329
for more synergy.

00:16:48.339 --> 00:16:51.309
They have a lot of things in common, putting things in

00:16:51.329 --> 00:16:52.339
common, always

00:16:52.359 --> 00:16:54.149
for the sake of each company benefit.

00:16:54.169 --> 00:16:57.649
If you maintain this kind of culture, extracted not from any

00:16:57.669 --> 00:16:58.669
book

00:16:58.669 --> 00:17:01.409
because there is no reference but extracted from common

00:17:01.429 --> 00:17:02.539
sense, you can

00:17:02.559 --> 00:17:06.970
go -- you can go very -- you can go very, very far.

00:17:06.990 --> 00:17:12.139
And frankly I think because Renault and Nissan and Japan and

00:17:12.159 --> 00:17:13.159
French --

00:17:13.159 --> 00:17:16.109
Japanese people and French people are so different that it

00:17:16.129 --> 00:17:17.129
was obvious

00:17:17.129 --> 00:17:19.200
for everybody.

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:22.690
When you start to see that, oh, you know, maybe the two

00:17:22.710 --> 00:17:23.710
companies are

00:17:23.710 --> 00:17:24.710
very similar.

00:17:24.210 --> 00:17:25.710
We're gonna merge them together.

00:17:25.659 --> 00:17:29.779
Now, here -- here comes trouble because there are multiple

00:17:29.799 --> 00:17:30.799
identities

00:17:30.799 --> 00:17:34.279
within each company and if you don't respect them, you gonna

00:17:34.299 --> 00:17:35.299
get in

00:17:35.299 --> 00:17:36.799
trouble -- you gonna be in trouble.

00:17:36.799 --> 00:17:39.799
That's why there was absolutely no merger with worked in the

00:17:39.099 --> 00:17:40.099
car

00:17:40.099 --> 00:17:41.099
industry.

00:17:40.349 --> 00:17:44.750
All of them are being sold, or collapsed.

00:17:44.769 --> 00:17:49.149
You know in look at Saab being sold, and Jaguar being sold,

00:17:49.169 --> 00:17:50.529
and Daim

00:17:50.549 --> 00:17:52.799
-- Chrysler, look what happens with this Chrysler after the

00:17:52.789 --> 00:17:53.789
grandeur

00:17:53.789 --> 00:17:55.789
story that we have been told in 1999?

00:17:55.589 --> 00:17:58.639
I mean, you have every single example which happened.

00:17:58.659 --> 00:18:02.399
It was not respected and it was not respected because it was

00:18:02.419 --> 00:18:04.509
violating -- violating common sense.

00:18:04.529 --> 00:18:06.279
We are the only surviver in this.

00:18:06.269 --> 00:18:08.019
And that's why people say why?

00:18:07.470 --> 00:18:09.220
When I ask the question of time.

00:18:08.379 --> 00:18:09.379
Yeah.

00:18:09.379 --> 00:18:12.129
It's a question of time before we gonna see problem.

00:18:11.879 --> 00:18:15.129
No, we not gonna see problem as long as we maintain the same

00:18:15.129 --> 00:18:18.629
pragmatic, prudent -- prudent approach to the -- to the

00:18:18.649 --> 00:18:19.649
lines.

00:18:19.649 --> 00:18:23.389
Carlos Ghosn: How do you identify leadership potential in a

00:18:23.409 --> 00:18:24.409
person

00:18:24.409 --> 00:18:27.159
and how do you attract and develop the best and brightest

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:27.750
people in

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:28.750
your organization?

00:18:28.250 --> 00:18:29.500
Carlos Ghosn: That's interesting.

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:32.250
There are some basic condition and if you don't see them,

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:32.500
forget about

00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:33.500
leadership.

00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:32.950
&gt;&gt;

00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:33.750
[Laughing]

00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:35.559
Carlos Ghosn: First one, very simple.

00:18:35.579 --> 00:18:36.579
Very simple.

00:18:36.579 --> 00:18:37.829
I have my first test.

00:18:37.619 --> 00:18:38.619
First one.

00:18:38.619 --> 00:18:40.369
If somebody doesn't listen, no way.

00:18:39.960 --> 00:18:40.960
Very simple.

00:18:40.960 --> 00:18:45.500
You sit down with anybody, you start to discuss etc., if he'

00:18:45.519 --> 00:18:46.519
s not

00:18:46.519 --> 00:18:51.119
listening to you, even when you -- and the test is, you

00:18:51.139 --> 00:18:52.139
start a boring

00:18:52.139 --> 00:18:53.139
conversation.

00:18:52.720 --> 00:18:52.920
&gt;&gt;

00:18:52.720 --> 00:18:53.720
[Laughing]

00:18:52.720 --> 00:18:53.720
Carlos Ghosn: Obviously, no.

00:18:53.720 --> 00:18:57.059
Because if you're very interesting it's very easy for your

00:18:57.079 --> 00:18:58.079
listening.

00:18:58.079 --> 00:18:59.079
Oh, no, no.

00:18:58.829 --> 00:19:00.579
You go for a very boring conversation.

00:19:00.079 --> 00:19:01.079
You know?

00:19:01.079 --> 00:19:01.279
&gt;&gt;

00:19:01.079 --> 00:19:02.079
[Laughing]

00:19:01.079 --> 00:19:06.720
Carlos Ghosn: And if the person really listens and really

00:19:06.740 --> 00:19:07.740
try, etc.,

00:19:07.740 --> 00:19:09.619
that's a very good start.

00:19:09.639 --> 00:19:11.139
A leader first is a listener.

00:19:11.119 --> 00:19:12.450
There it is.

00:19:12.470 --> 00:19:14.329
That's absolutely basic condition.

00:19:14.349 --> 00:19:17.849
If you're not a listener, you're never gonna -- you can be a

00:19:16.970 --> 00:19:17.970
leader

00:19:17.970 --> 00:19:19.970
but you're not gonna get very far.

00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:23.139
The second basic also condition is, I've never seen such a

00:19:23.159 --> 00:19:24.159
thing as a

00:19:24.159 --> 00:19:25.700
boring leader -- leader.

00:19:25.720 --> 00:19:26.720
Nothing.

00:19:26.490 --> 00:19:29.379
Leader is always somebody interesting.

00:19:29.399 --> 00:19:32.149
Somebody who can connect with you.

00:19:32.169 --> 00:19:33.169
Very important.

00:19:33.169 --> 00:19:34.169
Very important.

00:19:33.669 --> 00:19:37.819
I mean, so if I'm sitting with somebody and, you know, after

00:19:37.839 --> 00:19:38.839
15

00:19:38.839 --> 00:19:42.339
minutes I wanna go to the next meeting, I know it's -- it's

00:19:41.730 --> 00:19:42.730
not very

00:19:42.730 --> 00:19:43.730
good.

00:19:42.980 --> 00:19:48.039
So ability to connect, ability to be interested, and being

00:19:48.059 --> 00:19:49.059
interesting

00:19:49.059 --> 00:19:50.789
is also a very important feature.

00:19:50.809 --> 00:19:54.059
And you know this isn't something that you don't learn in

00:19:54.009 --> 00:19:55.009
school or in

00:19:55.009 --> 00:19:56.009
university.

00:19:55.259 --> 00:19:56.879
It is developed by yourself.

00:19:56.899 --> 00:20:00.569
Everybody has his own skills, etc. so I would say being a

00:20:00.589 --> 00:20:01.690
listener,

00:20:01.710 --> 00:20:05.470
being able to connect with people are two absolutely basic

00:20:05.490 --> 00:20:06.490
condition

00:20:06.490 --> 00:20:07.490
for leadership.

00:20:07.460 --> 00:20:11.490
For the rest, you know, efficiency, ability to communicate,

00:20:11.509 --> 00:20:12.509
openness,

00:20:12.509 --> 00:20:15.129
curiosity, intelligence, etc., that's fine.

00:20:15.149 --> 00:20:19.389
I have seen great leader who are not smart.

00:20:19.409 --> 00:20:26.259
You probably know enough of them that they are not smart.

00:20:26.279 --> 00:20:27.279
They're very common.

00:20:27.279 --> 00:20:27.480
&gt;&gt;

00:20:27.279 --> 00:20:28.279
[Laughing]

00:20:27.279 --> 00:20:29.029
Carlos Ghosn: No, but it's true.

00:20:28.779 --> 00:20:30.279
I mean, they're not smart.

00:20:30.029 --> 00:20:33.029
And we've seen a lot of people extremely smart who never --

00:20:32.279 --> 00:20:33.279
never were

00:20:33.279 --> 00:20:34.779
able to take any leadership position.

00:20:34.779 --> 00:20:37.029
So I don't think this is something discriminating.

00:20:36.779 --> 00:20:40.279
I have never sen a leader who is boring or at least at the

00:20:39.529 --> 00:20:40.529
beginning.

00:20:40.529 --> 00:20:43.029
He may be boring after -- after five or whatever and

00:20:42.529 --> 00:20:43.529
somebody who

00:20:43.529 --> 00:20:46.779
don't listen, who observe or try to see, okay, what's the

00:20:45.779 --> 00:20:46.779
situation in

00:20:46.779 --> 00:20:47.779
which I am?

00:20:47.529 --> 00:20:50.279
Carlos Ghosn: What role have mentors play in your life and

00:20:50.289 --> 00:20:51.289
what

00:20:51.289 --> 00:20:54.889
advice do you have for us in finding mentors in our careers?

00:20:54.909 --> 00:20:56.659
Carlos Ghosn: Oh, it's very important.

00:20:55.659 --> 00:20:56.659
Mentors.

00:20:56.659 --> 00:20:59.659
Very important particularly but they teach you what not to

00:20:59.679 --> 00:21:03.680
do.

00:21:03.700 --> 00:21:07.269
[pause] I had many bosses in my career because I started,

00:21:07.289 --> 00:21:08.289
you know,

00:21:08.289 --> 00:21:15.170
like a simple engineer and I learned as much with the --

00:21:15.190 --> 00:21:16.420
from the

00:21:16.440 --> 00:21:20.389
managers or the leaders who are making a lot of things which

00:21:20.409 --> 00:21:22.490
shock me

00:21:22.509 --> 00:21:25.039
as from the people who are inspiring me.

00:21:25.059 --> 00:21:26.559
Both of them are very important.

00:21:26.079 --> 00:21:27.079
Why?

00:21:27.079 --> 00:21:30.940
Because the guy, you know, who is your boss, and all of a

00:21:30.960 --> 00:21:31.960
sudden you

00:21:31.960 --> 00:21:34.960
say, well, you know, he doesn't communicate well, I'm not

00:21:34.240 --> 00:21:35.240
motivated,

00:21:35.240 --> 00:21:36.240
etc., you're learning.

00:21:35.990 --> 00:21:36.990
You're learning.

00:21:36.490 --> 00:21:41.730
You're learning the basics because you're gonna to always

00:21:41.750 --> 00:21:42.849
think every

00:21:42.869 --> 00:21:45.869
time when you will be in a leadership position, I don't

00:21:45.230 --> 00:21:46.230
wanna become

00:21:46.230 --> 00:21:49.559
like X, Y, or Z who were my leaders.

00:21:49.579 --> 00:21:52.829
I wanna make sure I'm interesting, I'm sure I'm associating

00:21:52.399 --> 00:21:53.399
people,

00:21:53.399 --> 00:21:54.399
etc.

00:21:53.839 --> 00:21:57.309
So the mentors are positive and negative.

00:21:57.329 --> 00:22:00.079
You have the people who are gonna teach you what are

00:21:59.689 --> 00:22:00.689
mistakes not to

00:22:00.689 --> 00:22:03.689
do and there are the people who are gonna inspire you by

00:22:03.359 --> 00:22:04.359
saying, well,

00:22:04.359 --> 00:22:07.359
I would have never thought about this and I think this is

00:22:06.569 --> 00:22:07.569
very, very,

00:22:07.569 --> 00:22:08.950
very powerful.

00:22:08.970 --> 00:22:14.730
So you learn from both and it's -- that's why it's very

00:22:14.750 --> 00:22:15.750
important to

00:22:15.750 --> 00:22:18.470
listen, and observe, and, you know, some people say, you

00:22:18.490 --> 00:22:19.490
know, I have

00:22:19.490 --> 00:22:20.740
a boring boss, you know?

00:22:20.740 --> 00:22:21.990
I'm not learning anything.

00:22:20.990 --> 00:22:21.990
Wrong.

00:22:21.990 --> 00:22:22.990
Wrong.

00:22:22.240 --> 00:22:23.609
You have a boring boss?

00:22:23.629 --> 00:22:26.129
It's an opportunity to see why he is boring.

00:22:26.149 --> 00:22:29.190
What are the things -- what are the things that I will learn

00:22:29.210 --> 00:22:30.210
that I

00:22:30.210 --> 00:22:33.710
will never have to do in the future so I am not boring for

00:22:33.210 --> 00:22:34.210
the people

00:22:34.210 --> 00:22:35.460
who are the my team?

00:22:35.460 --> 00:22:38.460
If you have a great boss from the beginning you think -- you

00:22:37.710 --> 00:22:38.710
gonna

00:22:38.710 --> 00:22:40.460
think it's very easy, you know?

00:22:40.210 --> 00:22:42.710
Because the guy's interesting, and the objective is being

00:22:42.429 --> 00:22:43.429
hit, etc.

00:22:43.429 --> 00:22:46.679
you're not gonna learn as much as if you would be facing

00:22:46.210 --> 00:22:47.210
adversity

00:22:47.210 --> 00:22:49.470
from the boss who has a lot of imperfection.

00:22:49.490 --> 00:22:53.419
Obviously if you -- if all your bosses are of this type, it'

00:22:53.439 --> 00:22:54.439
s bad also

00:22:54.439 --> 00:22:57.189
because you never know what's -- you know, what is true

00:22:57.189 --> 00:22:58.309
north.

00:22:58.329 --> 00:23:01.849
So having some of both is very -- is very important.

00:23:01.869 --> 00:23:05.190
I was blessed by the fact that I had both and frankly I

00:23:05.210 --> 00:23:06.210
learned as

00:23:06.210 --> 00:23:11.599
much from one than from the -- from the others.

00:23:11.619 --> 00:23:14.369
SPEAKER02: So while auto sales in the U.S. have remained

00:23:13.869 --> 00:23:14.869
flat or

00:23:14.869 --> 00:23:17.369
declined over the last few years, auto sales in many

00:23:16.869 --> 00:23:17.869
emerging markets

00:23:17.869 --> 00:23:19.869
continue to grow at a double-digit clip.

00:23:19.619 --> 00:23:22.519
How is this dynamic influenced Nissan and Renault, and how

00:23:22.539 --> 00:23:23.539
do you

00:23:23.539 --> 00:23:25.289
envision it impacting the global auto industry?

00:23:25.289 --> 00:23:28.039
Carlos Ghosn: Well, that's -- that's a very important factor

00:23:27.359 --> 00:23:28.359
because

00:23:28.359 --> 00:23:32.059
we -- we all know that the car industry is moving from north

00:23:32.079 --> 00:23:33.190
to south,

00:23:33.210 --> 00:23:36.269
and from west to east.

00:23:36.289 --> 00:23:37.289
[pause]

00:23:37.289 --> 00:23:39.609
In a kind of summary.

00:23:39.629 --> 00:23:42.259
The demand, obviously the United States, Japan, Europe, are

00:23:42.279 --> 00:23:43.470
gonna

00:23:43.490 --> 00:23:46.490
continue to be important market but I don't think growth is

00:23:46.379 --> 00:23:47.379
gonna be

00:23:47.379 --> 00:23:48.879
an important factor in these markets.

00:23:48.879 --> 00:23:51.419
Growth is gonna come from new markets.

00:23:51.439 --> 00:23:54.490
Obviously we all know China, India, the Middle East, South

00:23:54.509 --> 00:23:55.629
America,

00:23:55.649 --> 00:23:58.649
but also from the country of the future which are gonna be

00:23:58.069 --> 00:23:59.069
the next

00:23:59.069 --> 00:24:00.460
wave coming.

00:24:00.480 --> 00:24:06.559
Indonesia, Iran, Iraq, Vietnam, Mexico, some part of South

00:24:06.579 --> 00:24:07.759
America,

00:24:07.779 --> 00:24:09.919
maybe some countries in the Africa.

00:24:09.939 --> 00:24:11.539
This is the next brick.

00:24:11.559 --> 00:24:13.559
And, you know, we have a short memory.

00:24:13.309 --> 00:24:16.309
You know, I remember in 2000 -- in the year 2000, ten years

00:24:16.119 --> 00:24:17.119
ago, not

00:24:17.119 --> 00:24:20.139
so much.

00:24:20.159 --> 00:24:26.079
We used to sell 20,000 cars -- ten to 20,000 cars a year in

00:24:26.099 --> 00:24:27.829
China.

00:24:27.849 --> 00:24:32.889
China was maybe the number -- in the car industry it was

00:24:32.909 --> 00:24:33.930
market No. 20

00:24:33.950 --> 00:24:36.279
or 25.

00:24:36.299 --> 00:24:39.299
In 2009 it was the largest market in the -- in the world.

00:24:38.990 --> 00:24:44.389
And I think it's gonna be sustainable and we sold 700,000

00:24:44.409 --> 00:24:45.409
cars in

00:24:45.409 --> 00:24:48.329
China in ten years.

00:24:48.349 --> 00:24:51.099
And this is becoming one of the largest market of -- of

00:24:50.490 --> 00:24:51.549
Nissan.

00:24:51.569 --> 00:24:56.809
So today what I wanna know is, in ten years, what are the

00:24:56.829 --> 00:24:57.899
countries

00:24:57.919 --> 00:25:02.200
that's probably not like China but are gonna see this

00:25:02.220 --> 00:25:03.220
tremendous

00:25:03.220 --> 00:25:04.220
growth?

00:25:03.619 --> 00:25:06.669
So you look at the potential, you look at the resources, you

00:25:06.689 --> 00:25:07.689
look at

00:25:07.689 --> 00:25:10.909
the population, you look at the mismanagement.

00:25:10.929 --> 00:25:13.429
Usually the more the company is mismanage -- the more the

00:25:13.299 --> 00:25:14.299
company --

00:25:14.299 --> 00:25:16.799
or the country is mismanaged, the more potential it has,

00:25:16.250 --> 00:25:17.250
particular if

00:25:17.250 --> 00:25:18.919
it has natural resources.

00:25:18.939 --> 00:25:23.909
So you look at the leadership, uh, you look at the

00:25:23.929 --> 00:25:25.089
resources, and then

00:25:25.109 --> 00:25:28.109
you can start to list what are the countries which has the

00:25:26.759 --> 00:25:27.759
most

00:25:27.759 --> 00:25:29.259
potential for the next ten years.

00:25:29.259 --> 00:25:31.759
Some of them may not realize it because mismanagement may

00:25:31.259 --> 00:25:32.259
continue or

00:25:32.259 --> 00:25:35.009
aggravate but some of them are gonna fix their problems and

00:25:34.509 --> 00:25:35.509
then all

00:25:35.509 --> 00:25:37.509
of a sudden they're gonna be there.

00:25:37.259 --> 00:25:40.480
So Renault-Nissan, what you're trying to do is take all

00:25:40.500 --> 00:25:41.500
these

00:25:41.500 --> 00:25:44.000
countries which are the next generation of bricks and trying

00:25:43.559 --> 00:25:44.559
to

00:25:44.559 --> 00:25:46.950
establish a presence in them.

00:25:46.970 --> 00:25:50.220
Some of them will not bloom but the one who will bloom will

00:25:49.819 --> 00:25:50.819
be -- will

00:25:50.819 --> 00:25:51.819
be really worth it.

00:25:51.819 --> 00:25:54.450
SPEAKER02: Umm, what advice would you give to newly lamented

00:25:54.470 --> 00:25:55.509
MBAs and

00:25:55.529 --> 00:25:58.529
what mistakes have you seen them make in the early stages of

00:25:57.529 --> 00:25:58.529
their

00:25:58.529 --> 00:25:59.529
career?

00:25:58.929 --> 00:26:03.720
Carlos Ghosn: Uh, what advice I can give new MBAs?

00:26:03.740 --> 00:26:07.319
First I think -- I think the first one is that don't plan

00:26:07.339 --> 00:26:09.089
too much.

00:26:09.109 --> 00:26:09.309
&gt;&gt;

00:26:09.109 --> 00:26:10.109
[Laughing]

00:26:09.109 --> 00:26:12.859
Carlos Ghosn: Doesn't work.

00:26:12.879 --> 00:26:14.379
For me it didn't work.

00:26:14.079 --> 00:26:16.829
Frankly, don't plan too much your career because what your

00:26:16.569 --> 00:26:17.569
gonna be

00:26:17.569 --> 00:26:20.069
facing in life is probably more powerful and much bigger

00:26:19.809 --> 00:26:20.809
than you ever

00:26:20.809 --> 00:26:21.809
imagined.

00:26:21.559 --> 00:26:24.809
So if you're following your man, you may miss a lot of

00:26:23.549 --> 00:26:24.549
opportunity

00:26:24.549 --> 00:26:27.799
coming from the side but you may not even look say, oh, I

00:26:27.169 --> 00:26:28.169
need to

00:26:28.169 --> 00:26:29.169
continue on my plan.

00:26:29.169 --> 00:26:30.169
Okay?

00:26:29.419 --> 00:26:32.169
Even though on the side you gonna be huge opportunity coming

00:26:31.819 --> 00:26:32.819
you don't

00:26:32.819 --> 00:26:33.819
look at them.

00:26:33.569 --> 00:26:36.569
So don't plan too much or be flexible on the planning.

00:26:36.319 --> 00:26:39.069
You gonna have a lot of ordeal, particularly in the period

00:26:38.319 --> 00:26:39.319
we're

00:26:39.319 --> 00:26:43.119
getting in, 2010, 2020, I think there's gonna be a lot of

00:26:43.139 --> 00:26:45.639
transformation coming and there are gonna be a lot of

00:26:45.139 --> 00:26:46.139
opportunity so

00:26:46.139 --> 00:26:47.139
be flexible.

00:26:46.639 --> 00:26:52.169
Umm, no matter where you start -- you know, some of you have

00:26:52.189 --> 00:26:53.189
already

00:26:53.189 --> 00:26:56.609
jobs, some of you don't -- no matter what you gonna start

00:26:56.629 --> 00:26:57.679
with but if

00:26:57.699 --> 00:27:02.039
you really, really put your heart and it and your dedication

00:27:02.059 --> 00:27:03.059
in it, at

00:27:03.059 --> 00:27:05.559
the end of the day you always gonna be great.

00:27:05.559 --> 00:27:11.179
I never seen personally in my domain anybody working very

00:27:11.199 --> 00:27:12.199
seriously,

00:27:12.199 --> 00:27:16.019
wholeheartedly, with a lot of motivation, openness on

00:27:16.039 --> 00:27:18.460
anything and at

00:27:18.480 --> 00:27:20.480
the end of the day do not prevail.

00:27:20.089 --> 00:27:21.089
Never seen it.

00:27:21.089 --> 00:27:22.589
It's a question of time.

00:27:22.339 --> 00:27:25.339
It's a question of patience, a question of drive, that's

00:27:24.089 --> 00:27:25.089
very --

00:27:25.089 --> 00:27:26.089
that's very important.

00:27:25.839 --> 00:27:29.889
The third -- the third thing is it's also something very

00:27:29.909 --> 00:27:31.319
important.

00:27:31.339 --> 00:27:32.589
Don't work for recognition.

00:27:32.179 --> 00:27:32.379
&gt;&gt;

00:27:32.379 --> 00:27:33.379
[pause]

00:27:32.379 --> 00:27:36.720
Carlos Ghosn: It's an illusion.

00:27:36.740 --> 00:27:38.990
Somebody was saying, "If you want recognition, buy yourself

00:27:38.230 --> 00:27:39.230
a dog."

00:27:39.230 --> 00:27:39.430
&gt;&gt;

00:27:39.230 --> 00:27:40.230
[Laughing]

00:27:39.230 --> 00:27:45.210
Carlos Ghosn: Don't work for recognition.

00:27:45.230 --> 00:27:46.500
You gonna be disappointed.

00:27:46.519 --> 00:27:47.519
You gonna be disappointed.

00:27:47.389 --> 00:27:51.849
Work for yourself, obviously work for -- no matter what are

00:27:51.869 --> 00:27:52.869
your on

00:27:52.869 --> 00:27:55.369
objective, if you wanna become wealthy, if you wanna, you

00:27:54.869 --> 00:27:55.869
know, I

00:27:55.869 --> 00:27:56.869
mean, work for yourself.

00:27:56.869 --> 00:27:57.869
Work for yourself.

00:27:57.619 --> 00:28:00.369
I'm not saying that you need to be egocentric looking.

00:28:00.089 --> 00:28:05.440
No but I think do not put too much emphasis on the outside -

00:28:05.460 --> 00:28:06.460
- what the

00:28:06.460 --> 00:28:08.960
outside's gonna be bring you because you gonna be

00:28:08.439 --> 00:28:09.439
disappointed.

00:28:09.439 --> 00:28:10.439
You gonna be disappointed.

00:28:10.319 --> 00:28:13.569
And I wanna tell you why it's so important to hold this

00:28:12.569 --> 00:28:13.569
line.

00:28:13.569 --> 00:28:18.549
Umm, because when -- when you have to make hard decisions

00:28:18.569 --> 00:28:19.569
and probably

00:28:19.569 --> 00:28:25.500
some of you will have in the future, you gonna be alone.

00:28:25.519 --> 00:28:27.519
Do not think that this is a team.

00:28:27.470 --> 00:28:29.240
No, it's not true.

00:28:29.259 --> 00:28:32.509
At the end of the day, the guy who is gonna make the

00:28:32.379 --> 00:28:33.379
ultimate decision

00:28:33.379 --> 00:28:38.869
is one and this guy's gonna do it alone, and he's gonna do

00:28:38.889 --> 00:28:39.889
it based on

00:28:39.889 --> 00:28:42.639
his own value, and his own beliefs, and his own analysis

00:28:42.000 --> 00:28:43.000
transmitted

00:28:43.000 --> 00:28:46.750
by his team or whatever but at the end of the day he or she

00:28:46.549 --> 00:28:47.549
is doing

00:28:47.549 --> 00:28:48.549
the decision.

00:28:48.049 --> 00:28:50.799
And when you carry the decision, you're gonna be bombarded

00:28:50.230 --> 00:28:51.230
no matter

00:28:51.230 --> 00:28:52.849
what.

00:28:52.869 --> 00:28:56.710
