And, in fact, three questions.

00:38:27.909 --> 00:38:30.909
If you answer yes to the three question, then you say, okay.

00:38:30.500 --> 00:38:32.750
Zero emission cars gonna be part of the future.

00:38:32.389 --> 00:38:35.139
The first question is, do you think -- very simple -- do you

00:38:35.150 --> 00:38:36.150
think

00:38:36.150 --> 00:38:39.559
even though price of oil is unpredictable, do you think that

00:38:39.579 --> 00:38:40.579
there is

00:38:40.579 --> 00:38:44.539
more chance price of oil in the future go up or down?

00:38:44.559 --> 00:38:45.559
Okay.

00:38:45.559 --> 00:38:50.819
So, uh, if you say, yes, there is more chance that it goes

00:38:50.839 --> 00:38:51.839
up, well

00:38:51.839 --> 00:38:55.029
then, you are on the right path for electric car.

00:38:55.049 --> 00:38:56.299
If you think, no, no.

00:38:55.929 --> 00:38:56.929
This is fake.

00:38:56.929 --> 00:39:00.569
Oil, there is plenty of it and it is going to go down to

00:39:00.589 --> 00:39:01.589
$20, then

00:39:01.589 --> 00:39:03.339
even you should not even do hybrids.

00:39:03.339 --> 00:39:05.589
You should -- you should go back to gasoline engine.

00:39:05.339 --> 00:39:06.339
That's first question.

00:39:06.339 --> 00:39:09.279
Second question, do you think that the constrains on

00:39:09.299 --> 00:39:10.339
environment and

00:39:10.359 --> 00:39:13.500
the regulation on the environment are gonna become stricter

00:39:13.519 --> 00:39:16.650
or looser?

00:39:16.670 --> 00:39:21.069
If you say it's gonna become stricter, C02 emissions etc.,

00:39:21.089 --> 00:39:22.380
then you

00:39:22.400 --> 00:39:25.400
are also on the right path for the zero -- the zero emission

00:39:25.099 --> 00:39:26.099
car but

00:39:26.099 --> 00:39:29.599
it's gonna cost you more and more to emit C02 and this is

00:39:28.859 --> 00:39:29.859
something

00:39:29.859 --> 00:39:32.359
which is gonna make a difference between this technology and

00:39:31.609 --> 00:39:32.609
the

00:39:32.609 --> 00:39:33.609
others.

00:39:32.859 --> 00:39:38.630
And the third one is, more strategic -- strategic concern,

00:39:38.650 --> 00:39:39.739
which is,

00:39:39.759 --> 00:39:42.509
how much all the countries which are developing in the world

00:39:42.159 --> 00:39:43.159
are

00:39:43.159 --> 00:39:44.159
importing oil?

00:39:43.869 --> 00:39:45.509
All of them.

00:39:45.529 --> 00:39:50.480
China, the United States, obviously western Europe,

00:39:50.500 --> 00:39:51.500
obviously Japan,

00:39:51.500 --> 00:39:54.000
obviously -- but even China and India, which are the two

00:39:53.500 --> 00:39:54.500
power house

00:39:54.500 --> 00:39:57.500
coming, they are big net importers of oil and there is no

00:39:57.000 --> 00:39:58.000
chance, no

00:39:58.000 --> 00:40:00.500
chance this is gonna change for the next 30 years.

00:40:00.500 --> 00:40:03.480
So with all these superpowers -- they gonna be superpowers -

00:40:03.500 --> 00:40:04.500
- how long

00:40:04.500 --> 00:40:06.880
are we gonna accept that their transportation sector depends

00:40:06.900 --> 00:40:07.900
only on

00:40:07.900 --> 00:40:11.750
one commodity and they are net importer of this commodity?

00:40:11.769 --> 00:40:16.809
I remind you that if one major oil producer for whatever

00:40:16.829 --> 00:40:18.000
reason decide

00:40:18.019 --> 00:40:20.849
not to export oil -- and this happened in the past -- the

00:40:20.869 --> 00:40:24.039
transportation system of most of this country is paralyzed.

00:40:24.059 --> 00:40:26.309
That's why it is considered a strategic issue.

00:40:26.049 --> 00:40:31.389
So the only way -- the only way to dis-- disconnect this

00:40:31.409 --> 00:40:32.409
strategic

00:40:32.409 --> 00:40:33.659
issue is to bring electricity.

00:40:33.599 --> 00:40:34.599
Why?

00:40:34.599 --> 00:40:37.349
Because you can bring electricity out of oil, of coal, of

00:40:37.119 --> 00:40:38.119
natural gas,

00:40:38.119 --> 00:40:44.009
of nuclear power, of hydroelectric, of wind, of solar.

00:40:44.029 --> 00:40:46.029
You can do it literally out of everything.

00:40:45.900 --> 00:40:48.400
So if there is one commodity which would become very

00:40:48.289 --> 00:40:49.289
expensive or

00:40:49.289 --> 00:40:53.230
which become unavailable we can switch to something else.

00:40:53.250 --> 00:40:56.000
You can't in the case -- in the case of oil.

00:40:55.519 --> 00:40:58.829
So there are a lot of reasons for which, you know, we think

00:40:58.849 --> 00:40:59.849
that there

00:40:59.849 --> 00:41:03.690
is absolutely no doubt that the zero emission car gonna be

00:41:03.710 --> 00:41:04.710
part of the

00:41:04.710 --> 00:41:05.710
future.

00:41:04.960 --> 00:41:08.210
Now, the big question is, is it gonna be 10 percent in 2020,

00:41:07.920 --> 00:41:08.920
15, is it

00:41:08.920 --> 00:41:09.920
gonna be five?

00:41:09.670 --> 00:41:13.230
There is a lot of debate going -- going on.

00:41:13.250 --> 00:41:16.250
We are the most foolish today by saying 10 percent of the

00:41:15.400 --> 00:41:16.400
market in

00:41:16.400 --> 00:41:18.559
2020 will be zero emission.

00:41:18.579 --> 00:41:22.009
Frankly, I think the numbers will move up and all the people

00:41:22.029 --> 00:41:23.029
who are

00:41:23.029 --> 00:41:26.139
today we think is gonna be 1 percent, 2 percent, 3 percent.

00:41:26.159 --> 00:41:28.909
They're gonna make a kind of rolling forecast which mean

00:41:28.690 --> 00:41:29.690
every year

00:41:29.690 --> 00:41:31.190
they're gonna update the numbers.

00:41:30.799 --> 00:41:31.799
You know?

00:41:31.799 --> 00:41:34.299
So every day you don't know what their position.

00:41:34.299 --> 00:41:35.299
You know?

00:41:35.299 --> 00:41:35.499
&gt;&gt;

00:41:35.299 --> 00:41:36.299
[Laughing]

00:41:35.299 --> 00:41:38.049
Carlos Ghosn: So you -- we're gonna discover -- we're gonna

00:41:36.799 --> 00:41:37.799
discover

00:41:37.799 --> 00:41:40.799
at a certain point in time there are 10 percent who are

00:41:40.299 --> 00:41:41.299
probably the

00:41:41.299 --> 00:41:42.299
most conservative.

00:41:41.799 --> 00:41:45.130
It will take a very small crisis for all these numbers to

00:41:45.150 --> 00:41:46.150
change.

00:41:46.150 --> 00:41:53.170
It will take an environmental disaster, it will take an

00:41:53.190 --> 00:41:55.099
energy crisis,

00:41:55.119 --> 00:41:58.369
it will take a war in a country which is large producer with

00:41:58.319 --> 00:41:59.319
some of

00:41:59.319 --> 00:42:00.319
this control.

00:41:59.819 --> 00:42:03.389
So we gonna see these numbers gonna go up and frankly the

00:42:03.409 --> 00:42:04.409
likelihood

00:42:04.409 --> 00:42:08.309
that this happen in the next ten years, for me, probably is

00:42:08.329 --> 00:42:09.650
near one

00:42:09.670 --> 00:42:11.599
that you gonna have something happening.

00:42:11.619 --> 00:42:15.089
Even if it doesn't happen, it still makes a lot of sense.

00:42:15.109 --> 00:42:16.359
So we're gonna see.

00:42:16.109 --> 00:42:18.359
We have different opinions, we're coming with different

00:42:17.359 --> 00:42:18.359
technology.

00:42:18.359 --> 00:42:20.940
It's not either/or, you know?

00:42:20.960 --> 00:42:24.480
We have our hybrids but it is where do you put most of your

00:42:24.500 --> 00:42:25.500
resources

00:42:25.500 --> 00:42:26.750
in order to create leadership?

00:42:26.750 --> 00:42:33.360
SPEAKER02: I have a question over here.

00:42:33.380 --> 00:42:34.630
&gt;&gt; Hi, I'm Clay Calhoun.

00:42:34.380 --> 00:42:35.630
I'm an MBA one.

00:42:35.380 --> 00:42:38.130
Before I ask my question in interest of full disclosure, I

00:42:37.799 --> 00:42:38.799
worked on

00:42:38.799 --> 00:42:41.150
the automobile task force at the Treasury Department, uh,

00:42:41.170 --> 00:42:42.170
this summer.

00:42:42.170 --> 00:42:45.650
Umm, and so I'd like -- I'd really like your perspective on

00:42:45.670 --> 00:42:46.670
broadly

00:42:46.670 --> 00:42:49.420
how you think the restructuring of the U.S. auto industry

00:42:48.989 --> 00:42:49.989
has changed

00:42:49.989 --> 00:42:53.619
or hasn't changed the game for Renault-Nissan and, more

00:42:53.639 --> 00:42:54.779
specifically,

00:42:54.799 --> 00:42:57.420
returning to your comments on reliance, whether you think

00:42:57.440 --> 00:42:58.440
the

00:42:58.440 --> 00:43:01.460
Chrysler-Fiat alliance has a chance of success or is

00:43:01.480 --> 00:43:02.480
destined to kind

00:43:02.480 --> 00:43:06.480
of follow the previous alliances into problems.

00:43:06.500 --> 00:43:08.909
Carlos Ghosn: Uh, yeah.

00:43:08.929 --> 00:43:11.139
We -- are there any journalists in the room?

00:43:11.159 --> 00:43:12.159
No?

00:43:12.159 --> 00:43:12.359
&gt;&gt;

00:43:12.159 --> 00:43:13.159
[Laughing]

00:43:12.159 --> 00:43:17.869
Carlos Ghosn: It can be on the web site so we have to be

00:43:17.889 --> 00:43:18.889
careful

00:43:18.889 --> 00:43:19.889
here.

00:43:19.139 --> 00:43:20.139
That's all.

00:43:19.639 --> 00:43:19.839
&gt;&gt;

00:43:19.639 --> 00:43:20.639
[Laughing]

00:43:19.639 --> 00:43:20.889
Carlos Ghosn: I'm sorry.

00:43:20.639 --> 00:43:24.389
We are on the web site so I'm gonna have to be very polite

00:43:23.569 --> 00:43:24.569
and very --

00:43:24.569 --> 00:43:24.769
&gt;&gt;

00:43:24.569 --> 00:43:25.569
[Laughing]

00:43:24.569 --> 00:43:26.179
Carlos Ghosn: No.

00:43:26.199 --> 00:43:27.199
You know what?

00:43:27.039 --> 00:43:31.969
I -- I mean, I read -- I read the comment of Steve Rattner

00:43:31.989 --> 00:43:32.989
and, in

00:43:32.989 --> 00:43:35.989
fact, it happened that I was in a debate with Steve Rattner

00:43:35.469 --> 00:43:36.469
a few

00:43:36.469 --> 00:43:39.809
months ago in the Council of Foreign Relation.

00:43:39.829 --> 00:43:41.039
We were together.

00:43:41.059 --> 00:43:44.679
And Steve were very straightforward.

00:43:44.699 --> 00:43:46.739
He said -- he said --

00:43:46.759 --> 00:43:46.959
&gt;&gt;

00:43:46.759 --> 00:43:47.759
[Laughing]

00:43:46.759 --> 00:43:51.400
Carlos Ghosn: -- uh, General Motors we are not gonna abandon

00:43:51.420 --> 00:43:52.420
no

00:43:52.420 --> 00:43:53.420
matter what.

00:43:53.099 --> 00:43:54.829
Too much employment.

00:43:54.849 --> 00:43:55.849
Okay?

00:43:55.129 --> 00:43:57.089
So it was clear from the beginning.

00:43:57.109 --> 00:44:01.009
He said, "I've never seen people who are so polite and so

00:44:01.029 --> 00:44:02.029
arrogant at

00:44:02.029 --> 00:44:03.929
the same time."

00:44:03.949 --> 00:44:04.949
His comment.

00:44:04.389 --> 00:44:04.589
&gt;&gt;

00:44:04.389 --> 00:44:05.389
[Laughing]

00:44:04.389 --> 00:44:07.079
Carlos Ghosn: No, no.

00:44:07.099 --> 00:44:09.349
You know this.

00:44:09.369 --> 00:44:10.869
You've been part of it.

00:44:10.619 --> 00:44:13.119
He said it on record, it's on Fortune, etc.

00:44:12.869 --> 00:44:16.789
Uh, and he said that, uh, never seen a company which has

00:44:16.809 --> 00:44:17.809
been as

00:44:17.809 --> 00:44:22.519
mismanaged and where there is so much -- so few, uh, sense

00:44:22.539 --> 00:44:23.539
of

00:44:23.539 --> 00:44:24.539
emergency.

00:44:24.059 --> 00:44:28.489
But, you know, there is a new administration that could not

00:44:28.509 --> 00:44:29.509
let GM go

00:44:29.509 --> 00:44:31.989
because employment in that country, the impact on employment

00:44:32.009 --> 00:44:33.009
was huge.

00:44:33.009 --> 00:44:36.009
They said we had to do everything -- everything we had to do

00:44:35.769 --> 00:44:36.769
to save

00:44:36.769 --> 00:44:37.769
Germans.

00:44:37.019 --> 00:44:38.440
Okay?

00:44:38.460 --> 00:44:41.119
And frankly I think is very factual.

00:44:41.139 --> 00:44:44.500
Nobody, nobody in the industry -- and I can tell you because

00:44:44.519 --> 00:44:45.519
I've seen

00:44:45.519 --> 00:44:48.269
many bankers, and analysts and they came to -- and this was

00:44:47.769 --> 00:44:48.769
before the

00:44:48.769 --> 00:44:49.769
collapse.

00:44:49.019 --> 00:44:50.019
Two years before.

00:44:49.769 --> 00:44:53.179
Nobody would have predicted even in the wildest scenario and

00:44:53.199 --> 00:44:54.199
the

00:44:54.199 --> 00:44:58.190
wildest dream that General Motors would become majority

00:44:58.210 --> 00:44:59.210
owned by the

00:44:59.210 --> 00:45:00.210
U.S. government.

00:44:59.960 --> 00:45:00.960
No.

00:45:00.210 --> 00:45:01.210
Nobody.

00:45:00.460 --> 00:45:02.199
Nobody has seen this scenario.

00:45:02.219 --> 00:45:04.230
Nobody.

00:45:04.250 --> 00:45:05.250
Okay?

00:45:04.859 --> 00:45:07.859
So which mean that we have to be very careful when we

00:45:07.480 --> 00:45:08.480
imagine the

00:45:08.480 --> 00:45:11.909
future that it may always surprise us by what type of

00:45:11.929 --> 00:45:12.929
solution are put

00:45:12.929 --> 00:45:13.929
into place.

00:45:13.750 --> 00:45:15.000
This is for General Motors.

00:45:15.000 --> 00:45:19.569
Now, for Chrysler, back to Steve Rattner.

00:45:19.589 --> 00:45:23.469
He said it was 4951 -- no.

00:45:23.489 --> 00:45:24.489
It was -- yeah.

00:45:24.489 --> 00:45:28.539
It was 49-51 to let him go and he would give it to Fiat.

00:45:28.559 --> 00:45:29.799
His comment.

00:45:29.819 --> 00:45:33.319
And at the end of the day he didn't say exactly how it

00:45:33.289 --> 00:45:34.559
happened but

00:45:34.579 --> 00:45:37.329
probably inspiration is we have -- you have to let it -- you

00:45:37.179 --> 00:45:38.179
know, put

00:45:38.179 --> 00:45:42.460
it on the 51 and let it -- let it, uh -- let's give it a

00:45:42.480 --> 00:45:43.839
try.

00:45:43.859 --> 00:45:48.259
The bottom line of this is the major element here was end

00:45:48.279 --> 00:45:49.489
product.

00:45:49.509 --> 00:45:52.480
The major element here was protecting activities.

00:45:52.500 --> 00:45:56.269
It was not so much about potential on the market or

00:45:56.289 --> 00:45:57.289
competitiveness of

00:45:57.289 --> 00:45:59.389
the companies.

00:45:59.409 --> 00:46:01.659
And frankly it's totally normal because the French

00:46:01.670 --> 00:46:02.670
government moved to

00:46:02.670 --> 00:46:04.920
sort of guard the industry because of employment, Japanese

00:46:04.679 --> 00:46:05.679
government,

00:46:05.679 --> 00:46:10.289
uh, moved and put a lot of cash and liquidity during the

00:46:10.309 --> 00:46:11.389
dark days of

00:46:11.409 --> 00:46:15.440
the crisis in 2008 and 2009 because of employment.

00:46:15.460 --> 00:46:18.400
Everybody look at the industry with the prism of these guys

00:46:18.420 --> 00:46:19.420
are big

00:46:19.420 --> 00:46:20.420
employers.

00:46:19.670 --> 00:46:23.170
We can't just let it go.

00:46:23.190 --> 00:46:26.880
So this being said, this being said which mean that the

00:46:26.900 --> 00:46:27.900
companies have

00:46:27.900 --> 00:46:30.730
been supported not in function of their merit or their

00:46:30.750 --> 00:46:31.750
potential but

00:46:31.750 --> 00:46:34.250
because of how much damage this can create to the

00:46:33.929 --> 00:46:34.929
employment.

00:46:34.929 --> 00:46:39.509
Umm, in the industry there is no impossible nation in our

00:46:39.529 --> 00:46:40.630
industry and

00:46:40.650 --> 00:46:43.650
I'm really well positioned to tell you that because in 1999

00:46:43.549 --> 00:46:44.549
nobody

00:46:44.549 --> 00:46:47.549
gave a clue about Nissan being able to survive and we're

00:46:46.929 --> 00:46:47.929
doing very

00:46:47.929 --> 00:46:48.929
well.

00:46:48.829 --> 00:46:51.829
So I would -- I would not insult the future by telling you,

00:46:51.829 --> 00:46:52.829
uh, there

00:46:52.829 --> 00:46:53.859
is no chance.

00:46:53.879 --> 00:46:55.129
There is always a chance.

00:46:54.920 --> 00:46:58.509
Depends on how you manage, how much focus you put into it,

00:46:58.529 --> 00:46:59.529
and did you

00:46:59.529 --> 00:47:00.529
make the right decision.

00:47:00.529 --> 00:47:04.029
So I think -- I think it's still an open -- it's still an

00:47:03.029 --> 00:47:04.029
open story.

00:47:04.029 --> 00:47:05.779
SPEAKER02: We have a question over here.

00:47:05.469 --> 00:47:06.469
&gt;&gt; Good afternoon.

00:47:06.469 --> 00:47:07.469
Good afternoon, Mr. Ghosn.

00:47:07.469 --> 00:47:12.420
Excuse the getup once again.

00:47:12.440 --> 00:47:13.440
Given what --

00:47:13.440 --> 00:47:14.420
&gt;&gt;

00:47:14.440 --> 00:47:15.440
[Laughing]

00:47:14.730 --> 00:47:17.230
&gt;&gt; Given the comment that is you made about the differences

00:47:16.789 --> 00:47:17.789
between

00:47:17.789 --> 00:47:21.500
Nissan and Renault, and the demands on a CEO's time, and

00:47:21.519 --> 00:47:22.519
that

00:47:22.519 --> 00:47:24.769
synergies will be achieved and have been achieved across

00:47:24.199 --> 00:47:25.199
companies

00:47:25.199 --> 00:47:27.699
multiple different ways, it's not immediately apparent to me

00:47:26.819 --> 00:47:27.819
that

00:47:27.819 --> 00:47:30.230
having a single CEO is always the right choice.

00:47:30.250 --> 00:47:33.210
Why has that been an effective choice in this alliance?

00:47:33.230 --> 00:47:34.230
Carlos Ghosn: Yeah.

00:47:34.230 --> 00:47:35.730
I think you're totally right.

00:47:35.460 --> 00:47:38.710
I'm not gonna tell you that single CEO for two companies is

00:47:37.859 --> 00:47:38.859
the best

00:47:38.859 --> 00:47:39.859
choice.

00:47:39.109 --> 00:47:42.109
And, by the way, when the alliance started, there was no one

00:47:40.909 --> 00:47:41.909
single

00:47:41.909 --> 00:47:42.909
CEO.

00:47:42.159 --> 00:47:46.489
Louis Schweitzer was the head of Renault,

00:47:46.509 --> 00:47:47.759
[inaudible] was the head of

00:47:47.139 --> 00:47:50.389
Nissan, I came as the head of Nissan two years after I was

00:47:50.289 --> 00:47:51.289
CEO of

00:47:51.289 --> 00:47:53.690
Nissan, so Louis Schweitzer was heading Renault, I was

00:47:53.710 --> 00:47:54.710
heading Nissan.

00:47:54.710 --> 00:47:58.219
We were working together. in 2005, Louis Schweitzer wanted

00:47:58.239 --> 00:47:59.239
to retire

00:47:59.239 --> 00:48:03.069
and obviously he said, you know, you should be my successor.

00:48:03.089 --> 00:48:07.420
I would say, yeah, but the problem is, I'm not gonna abandon

00:48:07.440 --> 00:48:10.190
Nissan.

00:48:10.210 --> 00:48:13.460
So how can you be successor at Renault if you don't wanna

00:48:13.190 --> 00:48:14.190
abandon

00:48:14.190 --> 00:48:15.190
Nissan?

00:48:14.549 --> 00:48:19.539
Because I thought Nissan was still not completely, you know,

00:48:19.559 --> 00:48:21.569
reestablished even though the results were good, etc.

00:48:21.589 --> 00:48:26.079
So we come to the conclusion that I would manage both.

00:48:26.099 --> 00:48:27.349
Everybody thought it's crazy.

00:48:27.279 --> 00:48:28.279
How can you manage?

00:48:28.279 --> 00:48:29.279
Two different company.

00:48:29.029 --> 00:48:30.029
Two different yeah.

00:48:29.779 --> 00:48:31.900
Etc. etc.

00:48:31.920 --> 00:48:35.589
But I think this was the most reasonable solution not in

00:48:35.609 --> 00:48:36.609
absolute term

00:48:36.609 --> 00:48:39.089
but at least for the temporary period.

00:48:39.109 --> 00:48:42.380
When the crisis started, when the crisis started, I was

00:48:42.400 --> 00:48:43.400
realistic

00:48:43.400 --> 00:48:44.400
enough to say, okay.

00:48:44.269 --> 00:48:48.269
You can't manage completely being the COO, the CEO, and the

00:48:48.289 --> 00:48:49.289
chairman

00:48:49.289 --> 00:48:51.039
of both companies at the same time.

00:48:50.269 --> 00:48:51.269
You can't.

00:48:51.269 --> 00:48:54.019
So I've given up the COO responsibility by nominating one

00:48:53.769 --> 00:48:55.059
COO at

00:48:55.079 --> 00:48:56.989
Nissan and one COO at Renault.

00:48:57.009 --> 00:49:01.509
Shiga is chief operating office based in Tokyo, Pelata,

00:49:01.529 --> 00:49:03.199
Patrick Pelata

00:49:03.219 --> 00:49:07.059
is COO based in Paris, and they follow the day-to-day

00:49:07.079 --> 00:49:08.079
operation and

00:49:08.079 --> 00:49:11.079
they make sure that nobody's gonna say, you know what in

00:49:09.969 --> 00:49:10.969
where's the

00:49:10.969 --> 00:49:11.969
boss?

00:49:11.219 --> 00:49:12.469
We need an answer here.

00:49:12.489 --> 00:49:14.920
They're answering all the question connected with me.

00:49:14.940 --> 00:49:15.940
Okay?

00:49:15.940 --> 00:49:18.969
So I'm keeping CEO role and chairman of both company and

00:49:18.989 --> 00:49:19.989
delegating to

00:49:19.989 --> 00:49:21.630
the COOs.

00:49:21.650 --> 00:49:23.900
Is it gonna be like this in the future?

00:49:23.900 --> 00:49:25.150
I don't think so.

00:49:24.900 --> 00:49:28.799
We can come back one day in a situation where you have two

00:49:28.819 --> 00:49:29.819
different

00:49:29.819 --> 00:49:34.299
CEOs and you have the kind of board of the lines which is

00:49:34.319 --> 00:49:35.319
chaired by

00:49:35.319 --> 00:49:38.469
one of them or a third -- a third person.

00:49:38.489 --> 00:49:41.989
So I don't want you to think that this is the only solution

00:49:41.089 --> 00:49:42.089
to manage

00:49:42.089 --> 00:49:43.089
the lines.

00:49:42.589 --> 00:49:45.339
A lot -- I mean, we have been very, very pragmatic into

00:49:44.839 --> 00:49:45.839
shaping it.

00:49:45.839 --> 00:49:50.809
&gt;&gt; Umm, thank you so much for joining us today.

00:49:50.829 --> 00:49:53.829
I had actually had a similar question that was asked by this

00:49:53.469 --> 00:49:54.469
young man

00:49:54.469 --> 00:49:57.719
here and it's related to the goal -- the role of the public

00:49:56.969 --> 00:49:57.969
sector and

00:49:57.969 --> 00:49:59.969
the government in the industry in the future.

00:49:59.969 --> 00:50:02.469
You were talking about oil, which is an adjacent industry,

00:50:01.969 --> 00:50:02.969
which, 30

00:50:02.969 --> 00:50:05.719
years ago, was more than 75 percent privatized but today is

00:50:05.219 --> 00:50:06.219
more than

00:50:06.219 --> 00:50:08.969
90 percent owned by the public -- by the public sector and

00:50:08.469 --> 00:50:09.469
given what

00:50:09.469 --> 00:50:12.719
happened in the U.S. last year and also given that in China

00:50:12.219 --> 00:50:13.219
it's very

00:50:13.219 --> 00:50:15.719
typical for the government to force foreign players to have

00:50:15.219 --> 00:50:16.219
some sort

00:50:16.219 --> 00:50:18.969
of local joint venture, I was wondering how you think that

00:50:18.219 --> 00:50:19.219
might

00:50:19.219 --> 00:50:21.719
affect the dynamics of the industry going forward in the

00:50:21.219 --> 00:50:22.219
next few

00:50:22.219 --> 00:50:23.219
years.

00:50:22.469 --> 00:50:24.969
Carlos Ghosn: Well, you know, I personally was not shocked

00:50:24.469 --> 00:50:25.469
by what

00:50:25.469 --> 00:50:28.629
happened in 2008 and 2009, that the government intervening

00:50:28.649 --> 00:50:30.239
particularly to save employment.

00:50:30.259 --> 00:50:32.019
I was not shocked.

00:50:32.039 --> 00:50:33.289
I think it's normal.

00:50:32.909 --> 00:50:37.589
In a situation of crisis where there is no more rules where

00:50:37.609 --> 00:50:38.609
the whole

00:50:38.609 --> 00:50:41.609
system's shut down, somebody's gonna have to step and the

00:50:40.809 --> 00:50:41.809
market

00:50:41.809 --> 00:50:42.809
cannot step.

00:50:42.309 --> 00:50:44.539
I mean, only government can step.

00:50:44.559 --> 00:50:47.309
And why they intervened with the car industry they need to

00:50:46.259 --> 00:50:47.259
intervene

00:50:47.259 --> 00:50:49.609
with other industries just because they are large importers.

00:50:49.629 --> 00:50:50.629
That's it.

00:50:50.629 --> 00:50:53.629
The government we are driven by the fact that they don't

00:50:51.940 --> 00:50:52.940
want

00:50:52.940 --> 00:50:55.079
unemployment to go through the roof.

00:50:55.099 --> 00:50:56.349
That's a major motivation.

00:50:56.210 --> 00:50:57.960
They don't care about the cars.

00:50:57.710 --> 00:51:00.210
A lot of people -- they don't care about us.

00:50:59.960 --> 00:51:03.210
I say, okay, if I don't have a national producer, I will

00:51:02.599 --> 00:51:03.599
have somebody

00:51:03.599 --> 00:51:04.599
else.

00:51:03.849 --> 00:51:07.099
I mean, in the United States I would have no problem to let

00:51:06.849 --> 00:51:07.849
one or two

00:51:07.849 --> 00:51:10.099
companies collapse because we have so many in capacity

00:51:09.349 --> 00:51:10.349
existing

00:51:10.349 --> 00:51:13.809
competitors I'd be glad to take on this position.

00:51:13.829 --> 00:51:16.629
The question was employment and frankly not only the U.S.

00:51:16.649 --> 00:51:17.649
and I think

00:51:17.649 --> 00:51:21.149
it's totally normal and I was expecting it and I think it's

00:51:20.149 --> 00:51:21.149
sound that

00:51:21.149 --> 00:51:24.149
we don't give the impression to society that there is a

00:51:23.359 --> 00:51:24.359
problem, there

00:51:24.359 --> 00:51:27.400
is a shock coming, and everybody retires, or everybody

00:51:27.420 --> 00:51:28.420
hides.

00:51:28.420 --> 00:51:31.670
People have to stand up and face some of the problems and I

00:51:30.989 --> 00:51:31.989
think

00:51:31.989 --> 00:51:35.239
they've done the right things even though I'm not a public

00:51:35.069 --> 00:51:37.849
interventionist, I'm not a politician, but I think what

00:51:37.869 --> 00:51:38.869
governments

00:51:38.869 --> 00:51:42.250
have done during this crisis were the right things to do.

00:51:42.269 --> 00:51:45.719
Because when this crisis hit, all the companies were hit.

00:51:45.739 --> 00:51:48.109
The good ones and the bad ones.

00:51:48.129 --> 00:51:50.379
The competitive ones and the not so competitive ones.

00:51:50.059 --> 00:51:51.059
Everybody was hit.

00:51:51.059 --> 00:51:54.309
It's like, you know, you taking an athlete and you take a

00:51:53.559 --> 00:51:54.559
sick person,

00:51:54.559 --> 00:51:57.309
you put them in the room and you -- you stop oxygen.

00:51:57.309 --> 00:52:00.199
Well, both of them are gonna die.

00:52:00.219 --> 00:52:03.469
Maybe the sick guy is gonna die a little bit faster than the

00:52:02.710 --> 00:52:03.710
healthy

00:52:03.710 --> 00:52:06.960
guy but the healthy guy is gonna die also if you don't

00:52:06.199 --> 00:52:07.199
reserve oxygen.

00:52:07.199 --> 00:52:09.699
That's exactly what happened with the cash situation in

00:52:09.139 --> 00:52:10.139
2008.

00:52:10.139 --> 00:52:11.389
We were all under threat.

00:52:11.210 --> 00:52:12.710
It was a question of time.

00:52:12.710 --> 00:52:15.210
Government cannot stand -- say, okay, you know, we're gonna

00:52:14.859 --> 00:52:15.859
let the

00:52:15.859 --> 00:52:17.109
market forces -- what market forces?

00:52:17.109 --> 00:52:18.659
There was no more cash.

00:52:18.679 --> 00:52:20.480
The banks were not working, you know?

00:52:20.500 --> 00:52:22.250
There is no market forces at all.

00:52:22.250 --> 00:52:24.000
We just have to establish common sense.

00:52:24.000 --> 00:52:26.809
So I think -- I think common sense was established.

00:52:26.829 --> 00:52:29.609
Why some governments it took some time to react because

00:52:29.629 --> 00:52:30.629
frankly they

00:52:30.629 --> 00:52:32.539
did not know what was going on.

00:52:32.559 --> 00:52:35.909
I personally spent a lot of time with authorities in Japan,

00:52:35.929 --> 00:52:36.929
with

00:52:36.929 --> 00:52:40.639
authorities in France, to explain what was going on.

00:52:40.659 --> 00:52:43.199
And frankly this helps a lot for them understanding that

00:52:43.219 --> 00:52:44.219
there was not

00:52:44.219 --> 00:52:45.219
a manipulation.

00:52:44.789 --> 00:52:46.369
This was a real need.

00:52:46.389 --> 00:52:49.879
Federal government in the United States and -- and the Fed

00:52:49.899 --> 00:52:50.899
reacted

00:52:50.899 --> 00:52:53.649
very well because they started to listen to everybody what's

00:52:53.029 --> 00:52:54.029
going on.

00:52:54.029 --> 00:52:57.259
Tell us, when -- when is the cash re-established or not?

00:52:57.279 --> 00:53:01.489
I think -- I think most of the job done in 2008 and 2009

00:53:01.509 --> 00:53:02.509
there were

00:53:02.509 --> 00:53:05.569
mistakes but overall the reaction was sound.

00:53:05.589 --> 00:53:06.839
It's not visible today.

00:53:06.730 --> 00:53:09.480
Probably in five years down the road when we analyze this

00:53:09.170 --> 00:53:10.170
fact we will

00:53:10.170 --> 00:53:13.079
recognize the fact that many good things -- many good things

00:53:13.099 --> 00:53:14.099
happened

00:53:14.099 --> 00:53:15.099
during this period.

00:53:14.960 --> 00:53:16.210
So back to your question.

00:53:16.159 --> 00:53:21.379
I am not so favorable to public intervention into markets

00:53:21.399 --> 00:53:22.399
but I think

00:53:22.399 --> 00:53:24.399
there are two cases where it's necessary.

00:53:24.299 --> 00:53:27.549
The first thing is when there are no more rules. All of a

00:53:27.210 --> 00:53:28.210
sudden

00:53:28.210 --> 00:53:29.210
there is a collapse.

00:53:29.210 --> 00:53:30.210
Okay?

00:53:29.849 --> 00:53:31.170
Government has to step in.

00:53:31.190 --> 00:53:33.409
It was a case 2008-2009.

00:53:33.429 --> 00:53:36.750
The second reason is when you want to start something

00:53:36.769 --> 00:53:41.849
important.

00:53:41.869 --> 00:53:44.119
For example, I'm gonna give a technological point.

00:53:43.879 --> 00:53:46.129
Batteries technology today is something which we know is

00:53:45.739 --> 00:53:46.739
essential for

00:53:46.739 --> 00:53:49.000
the next 20 or 30 years.

00:53:49.019 --> 00:53:51.159
The research on battery is mainly concentrated between

00:53:51.179 --> 00:53:52.179
Japan, Korea,

00:53:52.179 --> 00:53:53.179
and China.

00:53:52.679 --> 00:53:57.210
The U.S. government, conscious of this, is saying this

00:53:57.230 --> 00:53:58.230
cannot be.

00:53:58.230 --> 00:54:00.839
We need to encourage development of research and development

00:54:00.859 --> 00:54:01.859
in the

00:54:01.859 --> 00:54:04.679
United States and they are putting money in it, and putting

00:54:04.699 --> 00:54:05.699
incentive,

00:54:05.699 --> 00:54:07.219
and encourage company.

00:54:07.239 --> 00:54:09.739
That's part of the job governments need to do.

00:54:09.379 --> 00:54:12.900
Recognize on a macro level that there is something big

00:54:12.920 --> 00:54:13.920
missing in the

00:54:13.920 --> 00:54:16.650
country and say, okay, we need to establish the incentive

00:54:16.670 --> 00:54:17.670
and the

00:54:17.670 --> 00:54:21.059
conditions to be able to bring back to the country.

00:54:21.079 --> 00:54:23.079
The Indian government is doing that, you know?

00:54:22.859 --> 00:54:25.109
I was in India a very long time ago.

00:54:25.109 --> 00:54:27.960
I say, there's no battery company in India.

00:54:27.980 --> 00:54:28.980
You know?

00:54:28.980 --> 00:54:32.289
India is proud saying we are the country of knowledge.

00:54:32.309 --> 00:54:33.309
Okay.

00:54:33.309 --> 00:54:34.309
That's great.

00:54:34.319 --> 00:54:35.949
Where is the battery technology?

00:54:35.969 --> 00:54:37.489
It's missing from India.

00:54:37.509 --> 00:54:40.509
And they are thinking about putting a kind of package to try

00:54:39.899 --> 00:54:40.899
to

00:54:40.899 --> 00:54:43.150
encourage company to move into the sector.

00:54:43.170 --> 00:54:45.170
This for me makes a lot of sense.

00:54:44.960 --> 00:54:49.039
These are the two conditions which you require governments

00:54:49.059 --> 00:54:50.059
to

00:54:50.059 --> 00:54:55.440
intervene and create the condition for the market to -- to

00:54:55.460 --> 00:54:56.460
start and

00:54:56.460 --> 00:54:57.460
to perform.

00:54:56.960 --> 00:54:59.710
SPEAKER02: Mr. Ghosn, thank you so much for being with us

00:54:58.960 --> 00:54:59.960
today.

00:54:59.960 --> 00:55:00.960
Carlos Ghosn: Thank you.

00:55:00.960 --> 00:55:01.159
&gt;&gt;

00:55:00.960 --> 00:55:01.960
[Applause]

00:55:00.960 --> 00:55:02.460
Carlos Ghosn: That's for me?

00:55:02.210 --> 00:55:03.460
So this is my size?

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.000
That's my size?

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.200
&gt;&gt;

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.000
[Cheering]

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.200
&gt;&gt;

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.000
[Applause]

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.500
Carlos Ghosn: Thank you very much.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.000
Thank you.

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:01.199
&gt;&gt;

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.000
[Applause]

